  "lookup_contract": [
    "Fresh inventory is actual source-existing identity evidence, not future selected PP applications or a final context.",
    "Unit selected app refs remain nil until actual source getter and ObjectReferenceAttribute setter. Parent Unit depth remains during application dedicated callback.",
    "Registry-missing false/true lookups both call synchronous SourceLookupRequest executor. Unregistered does not prove actual manager absence. False permits nil only after actual lookup; true requires confirmed object after creation/storage/observers. Registration preserves same objects and does not itself execute creation.",
    "Block application callback captures OLD group numeric address, probes CURRENT app target create=false, then fresh nil decision allows a CURRENT-app create=true getter and a SECOND CURRENT-app create=true getter whose result is assigned. Both later calls run even when the False probe finds an existing group. Creation/storage observers may change CURRENT app between getters. Primary Area accesses unused255 before block defaults, so subsequent blocks reuse that actual object.",
    "Missing installed decision and first create-enabled nil result remain explicit source boundaries; native nil fallback unused255 path requires its owning creation/observer executor rather than inferred success.",
    "Secondary application unused255 need not exist when raw Secondary mask0: no matching secondary block getter has run. Do not create it to fill a context requirement.",
    "Registration encounter order is not GroupManager Items order. Explicit actual-order binding validates exact registered manager rows; new registration invalidates order until source executor rebinds."
  ],
  "handoff_contract": [
    "Outer CoreKey update starts once; inherited Unit Init and nested update execute separately. At GetKeyBlocks Unitdepth1 remains.",
    "Retain SAME Unit/block/key/manager/attribute/owned target/subscription objects and current graph; no rebuilding from snapshot or raw final rows.",
    "Validate outer Unitdepth1 plus UnitManagerdepth0 and balanced primary/secondary/Area attributes, current primary-bound state0 empty keys, balanced block/key counters, canonical same-engine application/group pointers and source-established primaryunused255. Numeric identity equivalence does not admit foreign pointers. Preserve actual secondary object, including255 with no unused group.",
    "Application/raw request driver uses one outer runtime failure wrapper; native finally cleanup executes before runtime invalidation. Failed state has no resumed save projection."
  ],
